d 'FAILSAFE': module for postestimation statistical diagnostic linting
d
d  failsafe is a read-only postestimation command that inspects
d fitted Stata models for metadata and statistical conditions that
d may warrant review. It reports estimation-sample information,
d omitted terms, convergence status, variance-covariance problems,
d user-specified cluster-count thresholds, binary-outcome event
d counts, categorical cell structure, estimator-reported
d perfect-prediction metadata, and estimator-native Cox and
d Fine–Gray event counts when available. The command emits stable
d signal codes but does not refit models, select specifications,
d apply a generic events-per-variable rule, or declare a model
d valid or invalid. 
d
d KW: postestimation
d KW: diagnostics
d KW: model checking
d KW: logistic regression
d KW: survival analysis
d KW: competing risks
d KW: clustered standard errors
d
d Requires: Stata version 14.2
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260929
d
d Author:  Christina Laternser ,  Ann & Robert H. Lurie Children’s Hospital of Chicago
d Support: email christina.laternser.research@@gmail.com
d
f failsafe.ado
f failsafe.sthlp
f failsafe_examples.do
f failsafe_public_validation.do
